# Copy to deploy/.env (git-ignored) and uncomment what you need. Compose
# reads it automatically; run `scripts/yardctl up` after a change.

# Publish the three UIs on loopback only (single-host lab, or behind a
# local reverse proxy). Default: all IPv4 interfaces.
#YARD_BIND=127.0.0.1

# Postgres password. Only takes effect on a fresh bucket-dbdata volume;
# keep it URL-safe, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 24`.
#BUCKET_DB_PASSWORD=

# Initial bucket admin password, first start only. Unset: a random one is
# generated and printed once in the bucket log.
#BUCKET_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Behind a reverse proxy: its public origin(s), and its address or hostname
# so X-Forwarded-For/-Host are believed. Never list the yard network's
# subnet (see docs/SECURITY.md). The bucket always trusts syslog-hose and
# syslog-valve by name.
#YARD_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://yard.example.com
#YARD_TRUSTED_PROXIES=10.0.0.5
